{"ts": "2026-11-27T06:20:10.967802Z", "run_id": "r-20261127T0619Z-c7d9", "unit": "openspec:add-web-tool-trust", "seq": 5, "type": "human.verdict", "question": "Q-017", "target": "H-abcad329", "decision": "accept", "by": "delegate", "reason": "The unit can go on as it stands. The criterion pins what discoverBody does with a key that appears only in a draft's carried map: a key outside the pattern or one that brings the total over 100 throws RangeError, and otherwise the tool gets the overlay entry built from its carried fields. That is a builder result a browser cannot observe, because the pages fill carried only from discoverSettings of a stored surface whose server tool names storedTools has already checked against the same pattern, and from carriedAfterEffect keyed by a rendered row's name, so no page can produce a carried-only key that is malformed or in excess; an end-to-end test is not the right instrument. The Node test review-carried-keys.test.ts carries the criterion in its name and asserts exactly the scenario: RangeError for a carried-only key with a space, for an empty carried-only key and for 101 carried-only keys, and the body foo with name bar and unsafe_to_retry false for a well-formed carried-only key. The builder now adds the keys of carried to its key set before deleting __proto__, counting against 100 and testing each key against the pattern, then builds the entry from the carried fields through overlayEntry.", "text_sha256": "b20aa60404edd587fac4824fa6115a2ec52961165b153b230f1732f399e17f82", "answer_sha256": "5ac7878b287851eef4b1da3dfd119a8d1e42c521ce7ae72223ff12ab0988d42b", "profile": "delegate-fable", "model": "claude-fable-5-1", "cli": "claude-code"}
{"ts": "2026-11-27T06:20:10.969393Z", "run_id": "r-20261127T0619Z-c7d9", "unit": "openspec:add-web-tool-trust", "seq": 6, "type": "human.verdict", "question": "Q-018", "target": "H-1f2ad2b0", "decision": "accept", "by": "delegate", "reason": "The unit can go on as it stands. The generated browser test fails at the base and at the head for a reason of its own: it opens the registration page and at once expects a row for toString, but the Operations table renders only after an OpenAPI document is pasted and previewed, and the test never pastes one, so it fails against any version of the page and proves nothing about the code. The code satisfies the criterion. Every page reads its trust record through trustFor, which returns DEFAULT_TRUST unless Object.hasOwn finds an own entry, so toString or constructor with no own entry shows unchecked and with no data class; each setter writes a complete ToolTrust with trusted and dataClass, the data-class select maps its empty option to null, and the tick and baseline reads compare against true or read trusted of the inherited function as undefined, so a newly trusted prototype-named key is shown and must be ticked like any other. The OpenAPI builder reads trust and carried with Object.hasOwn, and discoverBody does the same, so the submitted overlay entry is the one overlayEntry builds for any other name and no RangeError arises. The Node test trust-lookup.test.ts carries the criterion and scans the three pages for a plain trust index with a nullish fallback and for the guarded lookup.", "text_sha256": "d4cce78df1df9359beda68a09d99d7847203ecdd26726f1666847ff0b3067ed1", "answer_sha256": "aa2bfd9fd6bce18fb6b214807ca61518533d9c4b1d90514323aca3c86dc900b5", "profile": "delegate-fable", "model": "claude-fable-5-1", "cli": "claude-code"}
